# local/ folder

The main repo ignores `local/`, so main-repo git commands do not track it.

- Never run a cleaning command in the main repo that would remove `local/`, such as `git clean -X` or `git clean -fdx`.
- Never add a remote to a repo in `local/`.
- Never `git add -f local/` or stage it from the main repo.

## Lockstep (only if `local/.git` exists)

- When you commit in the main repo, also commit pending changes in `local/` with the same message.
- Read-only commands (status, log, diff) need no commit in `local/`.
